  "details": "Immersion is a big staple for VR, people are always interacting in so many ways to immerse themselves in their environment and it could be a even more creative with the expression/fun of being able to go underneath things like tables, chairs, tunnels, and just about anything that is on a higher height than any small user's avatar.  ALL OF THIS being togglable as an option when creating a world while defaulting off.\n\nThis idea was inspired by other VR games where crouching and height can matter where you are going, and not to forget if you need a good idea of what I'm talking about involving where crouching and height matters, there is this one world on VRchat that is called  \"UDON Crouch test and stuff\"\n\nThey went in a good direction with the height adjustable dial and I can and imagine it going even further beyond with this suggestion, just imagine the sneakiness you could pull with being sly as a mouse going from spot to spot cause of a tiny gap.",
